<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Hardie says completes divestments.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Hardie says completes divestments.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Building materials producers James Hardie Industries Ltd said on Tuesday it had completed two major divestments.</p>
<p>Hardie announced in September it was selling its global irrigation business to U.S.-based Toro Co for about US$130 million.</p>
<p>The company said today the sale price had been adjusted to about $147 million (US$119 million) to reflect reductions in working capital in the seasonal business since March 1996.</p>
<p>However, this would not affect the net premium to book value which remained at $30 million, it said.  </p>
<p>Hardie also announced in November the sale of its fire protection and building automation operations to the Australian unit of Chubb Security Plc for A$220 million.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
